<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51553" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰωή</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>any loud sound: shout</i>, or
				<i>cry</i> of men or women, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ φρένας ἤλυθ᾽ ἰωή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.139
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦρτο δ᾽ ἰ. λεπταλέη ὀδυρομένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.708
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. δενδρώδης</span> (of Daphne)
				<i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				15.300
			</span></i>; <i>sound</i> of the lyre, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ δέ σφεας ἤλυθ᾽ ἰωὴ φόρμιγγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					17.261
				</span></i>
			; of the wind, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ Ζεφύροιο
			ἰωῆς</span> by <i>the roaring blast</i> of Zephyrus, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.276
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				11.308
			</span></i>; of fire, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρὸς δηΐοιο ἰωήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					16.127
				</span></i>
			; of footsteps, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποδῶν αἰπεῖα
			ἰ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				682
			</span></i>; <i>clang</i> of arms, <i><span class="en">
				Coluth.
				56
			</span></i>.—
				Ep.
			 word, once in Trag., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοᾷ τηλωπὸν ἰωάν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					216
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
